  "problem": "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+y=2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t+\u03d5)-t\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+\u03d5)+2t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t$\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t-2t\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $\u03d5$ are constants.",
